thank you for meeting with channel 8 to  discuss the world changer scholarship  that you offer at Hamilton and Manuela  orthodontics so we're here with both dr.  Hamilton and dr. Manuel II I hear that  you are approaching your fourth year of  offering this scholarship can you please  tell us a little bit about it absolutely  so the the world-changers scholarship it  started about four years ago and we  wanted to find a way to acknowledge what  some especially youth in the community  are doing to make a difference and to  make a positive impact and so we start a  scholarship and we heard that with a  calendar and so each year we search for  youth who are doing amazing things  around our community to make a  difference and we highlight them not  only with a scholarship but also with  recognition as as part of being part of  our annual calendar wonderful did you  have anything to add that to that as  well dr. Hamilton rocky what what I  really like about the scholarship is  it's just a continuation of who we are  and what we try to do we're in a  profession where we get to change  people's smiles and and and that changes  their lives but we find that they have  so much more to offer and when they go  out and do something that they have more  confidence and they can tackle the  things in life and reach for higher  goals that really just warms our heart  and we want more of that and if we can  facilitate it in some way I would say  the scholarship is just a continuing  effort on our part to help change  people's lives for the better and the  amazing thing that we find out about it  is we actually get more out of it than  the recipients so it's definitely a  win-win-win so we're looking for  applications for from students in any  student from kindergarten on up to a  senior in high school is is to our  primary audiences for the scholarship  and we've been impressed and amazed at  some of our younger applicants you know  kids in in grade school that are have  gone out of their way to make huge  differences in the community and  you don't have to be a senior in high  school getting ready to go to college it  can be anybody k12 can apply we've  always felt like there's everybody can  contribute and so we we want every  person that we meet or any applicant no  matter how large or how small that a  contribution it's it's kind of a it's an  effort by everyone if everyone can just  do their part it makes the world a  better place and so I would never want  anyone not to apply because they feel  they're not good enough or whatever  they're doing is not significant because  as we know every little bit helps we  wouldn't want anyone to think that their  contribution isn't great enough to apply  for our scholarship everybody can do  something  and no matter how large or how small it  often makes a much bigger difference  than you think so please apply where  where can we go to learn more  information about this program so the  best place to go is to our website so  that would be W WH AM ortho comm and  then you can just click on the world  changer link and there is it will take  you directly to the online application  where you can apply what made you decide  to start the world change your program  our scholarship dr. C why don't you  start on that and then all I in whenever  well first first of all rocky we're in a  great profession orthodontics is just an  amazing profession where we get to  change people's smiles and make them  feel a little more self-confident and  when you go dig a little deeper you  often get reminded that you're you're  literally changing their lives and then  they get to change the world and to be a  part of that we just felt like what can  we do to to get more of that and feel  more of that great feeling and so the  scholarship kind of was born out of that  so to speak when I was when I was young  I needed braces and one of the things  that I've always appreciated was that my  orthodontist took the time to explain  being with me and and specifically I  knew that  I knew that they believed I could do  everything that I needed to do to get a  great smile and so in the practice we  try to instill some belief especially in  our younger patient population that they  can do great things that they are great  that they're amazing  and if we can help them to believe that  about themselves we know that they're  going to continue to make a huge  difference whatever they apply  themselves to throughout their lives and  so we wanted to bring recognition bring  validity and bring really confidence to  these kids to help them to do those  great things which they want to do in  which they can do being an orthodontist  it's really a privilege to be able to do  what we do and we get reminded daily  that we're changing people's smiles and  improving them but but every once in a  while we get feedback that were actually  changed in their lives and that really  makes us feel good so we want more of  that and we've the scholarship was born  out of that how can we help young people  change the world and thus make us and  everyone else feel good about where we  are and what we do thank you so much for  joining channel eight and we look  forward to sharing this on our website  so for more information visit eight News  now.com and we will also link to the  scholarship application on our website  thank you for joining us today dr.  manolio dr. Hamilton
 

